==English==

===Etymology===
Compare {{cog|fr|spontanéité}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈspɒn.tə.neɪ.ə.ti/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-uk-spontaneity.ogg|Audio (UK)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|spontaneities}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The quality of being [[spontaneous]].
#* Elizabeth Browning
#*: Romney Leigh, who lives by diagrams, / And crosses not the '''spontaneities''' / Of all his individual, personal life / With formal universals.
# {{lb|en|countable}} [[spontaneous|Spontaneous]] [[behaviour]].
# {{lb|en|biology}} The tendency to [[undergo]] [[change]], characteristic of both animal and vegetable organisms, and not restrained or checked by the [[environment]].
# {{lb|en|biology}} The tendency to activity of [[muscular]] [[tissue]], including the voluntary muscles, when in a state of healthful vigour and refreshment.

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|quality of being spontaneous}} {{l|en|discipline}}

